ination findings are critical for diagnosis. Given the nature of SCFE, conservative management options such as reassessment, immobilization, or corticosteroid injections are inappropriate and could lead to serious complications. The most appropriate treatment for this patient is surgical pinning of the right hip to stabilize the femoral head and prevent further slippage or avascular necrosis. Immediate surgical intervention is essential in managing SCFE effectively. \n"], "raw_output": "'''Option: E'''"}
